WEBVTT

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.410
--Whoa! Huh? What?
--What's going on?
--What's all that shaking?

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.950
Will we be okay?

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.450
Th-This is...!

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.330
Earthquake?!

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.790
Quick, get under the desks!

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.450
I-Is it over now?

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.120
That was a pretty big one!

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.580
A-Are you guys oka-- Ow!

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.200
I'm okay compared to you.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.950
U-Ugh!

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.200
Oh, no!

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.500
Akari?

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.580
Thank goodness!

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.370
It survived! I worked so hard
to get my hands on this!

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.620
Th-That's nice.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.950
Is everyone else all right?

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.910
That wasn't nearly as scary as mice!

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.700
Yup! I'm perfectly fine!

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.200
No problems here either!

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.620
Thank goodness. Huh? What?

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.700
Mineko?

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.160
What's the matter, Mineko?

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.830
There's a smell.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.370
Smell?

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.700
The smell of shinies.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.750
Huh?

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:33.620
This way.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:34.620
Huh?

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.040
Mineko, wait! Hold up!

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.620
W-We should go too!

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.870
Anything could happen, so take everything!

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.080
Right!

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.200
Guide, please hold the fort!

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.750
Roger that!

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:03.540
Do you think they'll be okay, old man?

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.750
<i>Let's dive right into today's letters</i>

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:19.250
<i>It's "Personal Advice" and the title is</i>

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.250
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.830
<i>Hey, hear me out.</i>
<i>There's something I really wanna say</i>

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:41.080
<i>You've got courage to follow</i>
<i>your dreams which is why I chose you</i>

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.200
<i>Is it a risky bet</i>

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.660
<i>Despite no experience,</i>
<i>we jumped right in together</i>

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.120
<i>And this unpredictable story</i>

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:58.200
<i>Is your creation--</i>
<i>a heart-throbbing innovation</i>

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.660
<i>Quickly! Quickly! Take me along</i>

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.290
<i>On a bittersweet love venture</i>

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:08.080
<i>Ah! Measured not by skill</i>
<i>but by scale and romance</i>

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.120
<i>Hurry! Hurry! Boldly, subtly, show your appeal</i>

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.200
<i>Ah! Our meeting was a miracle</i>
<i>that can't be neglected</i>

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.790
<i>It's galactic level</i>

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:25.290
<i>I see. Sounds like you're head over heels.</i>

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.580
<i>Let's tell him, just like battle</i>

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.950
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.330
<i>Everyone, Hurry! Hurry Love! Love!!</i>

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:44.910
"Episode Eleven: Business Opportunity"

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.410
Huh?!

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.330
Wh-What in the world?!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.200
There never used to be a dungeon here, right?

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.750
Yeah. It was always just forest here.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:06.410
Then, what gives? Someone make this overnight?

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:10.330
No way. It's not some pop-up hotel.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:15.000
What if this place is like that
weird dungeon we explored?

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.410
You mean... the one with maju corporate slaves?

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:24.910
Yeah. It looks kinda similar, and that gate
appeared out of nowhere too.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.040
Don't you agree, Yutoria?

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.160
Yeah. That's true.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.580
In that case, I'd rather not be here.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.000
I'm still traumatized.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.830
Smell of lots of shinies come from inside.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.000
--Huh?
--What?!

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.500
Really, Mineko?

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:47.040
Yeah. Lots more than Mineko gathered.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.290
R-Really?! There's really that much kirakuri?!

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.160
Y-Yeah.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.500
What's gotten into you, Yutoria?

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:02.830
It's enough! With that much kirakuri,
we'll be able to summon the goddess!

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:04.370
You mean...?

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:07.830
We'll be able to find out my dad's whereabouts.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:08.830
Right!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.040
President? What's our plan?

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.160
Let's go!

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.540
Not just because of my dad,
but because we're adventurers!

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:25.830
We go wherever there's kirakuri!

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:30.660
That's right! Let's just hope there're
no maju corporate slaves.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.500
If we're going in, I'm right behind you.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.870
Me too. After all, Mineko found this dungeon.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.080
Mineko goes with Makoto.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:47.160
This is a huge chance for our company!
It's a business opportunity!

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.500
Yup!

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.660
We're doing it, President!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:54.950
All right! Let's get pumped up
and get this show on the road!

00:05:54.950 --> 00:06:00.000
Guys! It's been a while, but c'mon!
Say it with me!

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.750
Kibou...

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.750
...Fight!

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:07.120
Yay...

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.500
N-Not this again...

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:21.700
A business grade of "C"?

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:26.330
I don't agree! I simply
don't agree with this one bit!

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:30.200
It's because we haven't gotten any kirakuri lately.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.950
We're in dire need of a haul.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:36.750
Yeah. And nobody's been
through this dungeon yet.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:40.910
We'll jump a few ranks and
become a top-class company!

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:45.830
But, Rivar... You forgot some of your equipment!

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.830
What happened to that tiara of yours?

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:53.790
Like hell I'd wear that!
I'm pissed just thinking about it!

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:57.370
Jeez! I can't believe what
those guys put me through!

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.120
Gah! They're here?!

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.950
Way to be annoying as usual.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.200
Rivar! Thanks for the help the other day!

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.950
We even came out with a new employee!

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:09.660
Mineko hates him.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.080
Hey! That's blunt!

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:17.120
Oh, my. Hello there, Minato! Long time no see!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.120
V-Valmi? It's been a while.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.080
A rival has appeared, huh?

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.660
But... We're not gonna lose!

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:31.200
The same goes for us!

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:36.000
But the thing is, we're not the
only ones who came to the party.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.000
What?

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.290
Huh? When did she...?

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.790
Hmph! She's here too?

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.500
Hey, who's that?

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:51.080
An employee of one of the best.
She works for Imperial.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:57.000
She was in a contest we entered
and beat both us and Rivar.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.370
If I recall, her name is...

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.500
Subaru.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.120
So long.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.790
Hey! Wait up, lady!

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:10.750
Sheesh! She got a head start
on us because of you!

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:14.000
S-Sorry! I didn't mean-- Sorry!

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.080
Whatever! I refuse to lose this time!

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:19.410
I'll help you get revenge!

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:23.500
Yup! Last time was frustrating!

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:24.790
Let's go, President!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.330
Jeez! I said I was sorry...

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:39.120
She's so fast! That's Imperial for you!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.200
Cyedge is here too, so we really need to hurry.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.870
Mineko, can you smell kirakuri?

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:48.410
Yeah. This way.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:52.790
I'm not sure why, but this dungeon
feels so weird to me.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:58.200
Yeah. It's mechanized here and there
but old fashioned at the same time.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.660
It's eerily majestic.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:05.870
Like the president was saying,
this might tie into the Big Gate.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:07.660
Sure seems like it.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:11.250
What do you think's happening in the Big Gate?

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.500
That's...

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:17.540
Whoa! Look out!

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.160
Not these guys!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.540
It's them again!

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:24.830
--Workplace harassment...
--Low wages... Low wages...

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.660
Don't you think they're acting weird?

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:31.000
They don't seem as lively as before.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.290
You're right.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:36.790
I don't see their boss either.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:41.290
Hmph! This won't go like it did last time!
Prepare yourselves!

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:46.950
Bring it on! I'm gonna give you
a taste of my real power!

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:49.450
Th-They really were traumatized...

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.790
Um, well...

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.370
Mineko will handle.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:55.790
Huh?

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.160
Mineko!

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.750
Careful! They'll make you a corporate slave!

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:07.160
Wage theft... Wage theft...

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.330
Early retirement!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.790
Th-Thanks, Mineko.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.040
You're "velcome"!

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:17.830
You guys okay?

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:18.830
Mm-hmm!

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:24.500
In that case, let's hurry up.
Mineko, is the kirakuri this way?

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.950
Yeah. Smell is ahead.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:31.290
Did their boss from before get demoted?

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.660
He was pretty oppressive, but...

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:37.000
These maju seem worse off than before.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.660
I wonder where their current boss is.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:43.700
I think we'll find the answer if we keep going.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.370
Guys, be especially careful from here on out.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:51.410
There might be traps just like the last dungeon.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:53.200
Hmm? What?

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:54.200
President!

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.330
Wh-What is it this time?!

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:01.500
Yutoria!

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:12.160
Yutoria! Yutoria!

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:15.910
Yutoria, you okay?!

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:20.250
Wow, that was a scare!

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.910
Mineko, you okay?

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.910
Yeah. Fine.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.750
Huh? Where's the president?

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:29.040
We're over here!

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.540
I'm fine! And Yutoria... She seems okay!

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.330
How about you?!

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:40.290
We're okay over here,
but we're totally blocked off from you!

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:44.080
That's a problem.
I doubt we can break this wall either.

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:46.790
What do we do, President?

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:50.080
Mineko! Can you still smell kirakuri?!

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:52.620
Yeah. Shinies are deeper.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:54.700
President! They're deeper!

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:58.790
In that case, I think we should
just keep on going, right?!

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:01.660
Yeah! Cyedge might beat us to it!

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:04.290
We'll keep pushing onward then!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.540
Okay! Let's meet up later!

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:07.870
Can you stand?

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.200
Y-Yeah.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.000
Let's go.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.620
I wonder if those two will be okay.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:27.080
They'll get along just fine. Yutoria's with him.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.830
They'll get along and then some!

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:33.000
Jeez. Everything you say is so cheeky.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.450
Well, I guess he's gotten us out of a few pickles.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:41.000
And his battle orders are so good,
we can always count on him.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.160
I count on Makoto.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.370
Really? Thank you!

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.040
Good grief. Listen to these guys...

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:51.330
Uh, it's time to put the flirting on hold.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:56.870
A three-headed maju!

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:01.160
The tough one from the contest?
It looks weaker though...

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.290
What now? Turn around?

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:06.910
There's no need for that! After all...

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:09.790
We're a lot stronger than before!

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:12.370
Okay! Same strategy?

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.290
Huh? What strategy?

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:25.950
Hey! I guess you breathe fire,
but it won't hold a candle to my magic!

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:31.370
My magic is super amazing!
It'll make your eyes pop out of your head!

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:35.000
So if you don't wanna get hurt,
you better behave!

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:42.750
When a lady tells you something...

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.660
...you oughta listen!

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:51.330
Marika's going all out! But now, it's our turn!

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:52.540
You ready?!

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:05.080
What's wrong, President?
You seem different than usual.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:09.290
Huh? You think? I'm not sure
why you would say that.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:11.750
Are you not feeling well?

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:14.830
You did stay up late taking care of me.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.830
Huh?

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:22.200
Hmm... You're a little hot after all.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:26.330
Th-That's not from me being sick!

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.330
Then, what could it possibly be from?

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.290
'C-Cause, you're...

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.290
Huh?

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:37.540
--Wh-When did you...?!
--U-Um, this is...!

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.250
Don't let us stop you.

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:41.620
Please, carry on!

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:44.000
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.910
That's right! She was checking
if I had a high temperature!

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.700
It was getting real steamy all right!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:54.330
Could you not be so clever at a time like this?!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:59.410
You being a thing is a company secret, huh?
Now we know!

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.410
I'm saying it's not like--

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:04.410
Now, now. More importantly...

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:07.120
Shall we explore the rest together?

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.910
What? Why pair up with them?

00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:12.450
I think it's a great idea!

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:15.790
As they say, the more the merrier!

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:19.080
Ahem! What do we do, President?

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:25.290
I'm the only fighter between us,
so it might help us out if we join them.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:27.000
R-Right.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.950
I guess it's settled then!
Let's continue onward!

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:55.700
Hmph! Grouping with a lowly
two-star boss and his secretary...

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:58.950
I much would've preferred Akari.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.330
Sorry.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.160
Don't apologize for that, President!

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.660
S-Sorry!

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:09.120
But, hey! It's true I only have two stars!

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:10.870
That's not the point.

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:15.120
Don't you worry!
Any friends of Akari I'll protect!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.040
Just make sure to stick by my side!

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:22.750
Rivar, there's really no need
to be so accommodating.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.790
Huh? What do you mean?

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:29.120
What I'm saying is,
they don't need your protection.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:32.250
After all, Minato is...!

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.370
Yeah? What about him?

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:37.540
You see, Minato is...!

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:39.250
--Oh, my!
--Huh?

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:40.540
It's maju!

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:45.410
--No vacation... No vacation...
--Stress... Stress...
--Workplace harassment...
--Low wages... Low wages...

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:48.330
Gah! These guys?!

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.200
There's a hell of a lot too!

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:56.830
I'll take command! Rivar, defend from
the front and distract the enemy!

00:16:56.830 --> 00:17:00.450
Yutoria and Valmi should flank them from behind!

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:01.660
Got it, President!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.500
Roger that!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:08.000
Tsk! I don't like it much, but oh, well!

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:14.870
Nice! That was easy this time!

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:18.830
It seemed tired or something.
That wasn't tough at all!

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:23.660
It was pretty smart to have
the three heads fight each other!

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.450
Yeah. The president taught us that.

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:31.830
The president? Then he's smarter
than he looks with that dumb face of his.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:34.250
Who is President?

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.830
I'm not sure what to tell you.

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:40.870
He's the old man's son
and a two-star adventurer.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:43.790
Huh? Just two stars? That's low!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:48.080
Yeah. It seems ridiculous
when you think about it, right?

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.290
Hmm. A man of mystery.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:55.250
Speaking of which, what did he do
before he became president?

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.250
I heard he was a NEET.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:58.950
And before that?

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.830
Hmm? Before that?

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:04.080
Oof!

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.330
Hmm?

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:09.250
Oh, my! We won't be tidy
with papers lying around!

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:15.450
The president's resume, huh?

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.080
This sure brings back memories!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.120
This is the end for you!

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:31.000
Clocking... out... for... good...!

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.580
Nice! You're pretty good, Rivar!

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.620
Yeah. I kinda am.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:41.910
Your battle orders made it so easy.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:48.500
Not even our CEO-class people can
command battles as smoothly as you.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:52.040
Whoa! Did you hear that, President?!

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:53.790
Y-Yeah!

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:57.500
Are you really ranked two stars
like you say you are?

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.700
Huh? I am, but...

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:06.160
Yeah? Even Rivar is starting to notice now!

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:10.660
That is, how Minato is no ordinary person!

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:12.370
Don't make fun of me.

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:14.040
What are you getting at?

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:19.040
I'm saying that Minato
is exceptionally talented!

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.700
But he seems to be hiding his history from us.

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:26.200
Hiding his history? But why would he?

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:29.660
I can think of lots of reasons for it!

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:32.120
For example...!

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:35.620
Like having a past he doesn't want us to know!

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:37.830
He doesn't want us to know?

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:42.540
Minato? Do you remember
what I said to you before?

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:46.540
About a certain elite employee, that is!

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:49.080
I've heard rumors going around.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:53.450
That an elite employee recently
left a certain top company.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:59.290
You see, I did a little research of my own!

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:05.120
And in the end, I discovered
that employee was you after all!

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:08.290
Minato? What does she mean?

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:11.410
How come you didn't tell anybody?

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:14.580
The truth is, you used to work at Imperial!

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.200
--Huh?!
--Wha--?!

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:18.410
Imperial?! Him?! At <i>that </i>company?!

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.200
I-Is it true, President?

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.830
Y-Yeah.

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:28.370
That's not something you had to hide.
Why didn't you say?

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:30.950
B-Because...

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:36.330
Minato couldn't have told you
even if he wanted to!

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:38.620
After all...

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:41.750
...he was fired for workplace violence.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:48.000
This puny guy got violent?
You gotta be kidding me!

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:51.250
I'm sorry to say it's the truth.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:55.080
It's become quite the rumor, actually!

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:57.120
You...?

00:20:57.120 --> 00:21:00.790
President? No, Minato...

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:04.410
What's this about workplace violence?

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:06.870
Hey, Minato! Answer me!

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.290
President!

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.200
We're glad you're safe!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:16.040
I told you! We didn't have to worry about 'em!

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.120
We fought a three-headed maju,

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:21.620
but it was a piece of cake
with the method you showed us!

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:24.830
I'm surprised you thought
of a strategy like that!

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:26.950
Y-Yeah.

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:31.250
Marika's magic was incredible!
I wish you could've seen it!

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.250
And even Mineko was--

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:34.950
Makoto! Something coming!

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:36.160
Huh?

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:38.580
Terrible smell coming closer!

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:40.000
A terrible smell?

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:44.370
What the--? What's that sound?!

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.620
Shoot! Everyone, get--

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:04.250
Minato!

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:43.250
<i>Looking way up into the night sky</i>

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:47.870
<i>A pretty jewel caught my eye</i>

00:22:47.870 --> 00:22:52.200
<i>Clear skies tomorrow sure would be nice</i>

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:56.330
<i>Now, make a wish upon a star</i>

00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:58.410
<i>Lazily</i>

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:01.250
<i>Today comes to a close</i>

00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:05.620
<i>Dead tired and worn out</i>

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:12.120
<i>Good work</i>
<i>Let's do our best again tomorrow</i>

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.700
<i>Goodnight</i>

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.870
<i>Every day is sparkling</i>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:21.410
<i>Just like a box of jewels (sparkling)</i>

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:23.620
<i>And so brilliant</i>

00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:25.830
<i>Any work undone</i>

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:30.410
<i>We'll leave for dreamland (sleep tight)</i>

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:33.910
<i>Let's embark on adventure</i>

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:38.200
<i>So sleep soundly tonight</i>

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:43.450
<i>And meet up with me in our dreams</i>

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:46.540
<i>Sleep tight</i>
